# Upstream tests a pre-release build does not run: one path per line,
# relative to the upstream tree, then what makes the line removable.
# build/build-deb.sh drops the execute bit of each, and upstream's runner
# runs executables only.
#
# For a test that fails for a reason upstream has to fix, not this
# packaging: the build would otherwise fail most nights on something a
# rebase here cannot change. Every line names the upstream pull request or
# issue whose merge deletes it.

# showgraph crashes on about one failed graph in two hundred on Debian 12
# (Pango 1.50.12), so this test of 200 fails there more often than not.
# Fixed by xymon#1024. A preview is cut from main at one moment, so the
# line stays until that is merged and the newest preview has it as well.
tests/web/showgraph-rrd-error-exit.sh	xymon#1024, in main and in the newest preview

# Checks that xymonserver.cfg.DIST sets XYMSRV to loopback. Debian's
# 12_hobbitvars.patch takes XYMSRV out of that file and includes one that
# sets it, and the test has skipped in that case since xymon#435 merged on
# 2026-11-24. preview-4.3.32-5 was made two days earlier and carries the
# test without the skip, so it fails there; on main the line changes nothing.
tests/server/serverconfig-local-client.sh	a preview newer than preview-4.3.32-5
